WEBVTT

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.190
Blue sky!

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.180
Blue sea!

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.140
Let's have some summer fun!

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.860
Yahoo!

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.420
Hinata-chan, that's cold!

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.290
Take that!

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.380
Akari!

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.690
Caught you!

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.080
It's coming your way!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.740
I got it!

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.720
<i>What kind of harassment is this?</i>

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.020
<i>Thus the vampire becomes even paler...</i>

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.480
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.480
<b>Summer Break Spent with a Vampire</b>

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.670
What do you think, Sophie-chan?

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:19.840
It's the sea!

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.980
Are you having fun?

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.370
How could I be?!

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.650
Sunlight...

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.650
Running water...

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.250
When I woke up, I found myself 
surrounded by my mortal enemies.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:36.460
Akari, please explain why 
I'm in such a place.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.500
You said you'd never been to the beach before.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.570
And now it's finally summer break.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.850
And... there.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.060
Your bag's awfully large.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.540
So you brought me here while I was asleep?

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.660
You didn't notice?

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.440
You even have a swimsuit on, 
so I thought you were totally into it!

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.070
I have a vague recollection of 
changing while I was half-asleep.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.420
I slept really well, since 
something was rocking me.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.460
Vampires sure do sleep deeply.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.290
W-Was this a bad idea?

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:12.090
I did bring your parasol 
and cloak, but I guess

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.240
it's still not okay?

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.510
Of course it's not okay!

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.460
Even now, I'm surrounded 
by danger on all sides!

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.580
I didn't know you didn't 
get her permission.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.910
Even for a surprise, 
you took this way too far.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.220
She's partially to blame for 
sleeping through it, but...

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.710
I just wanted to enjoy my 
summer break with you.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.600
I invited Ellie, too, but she said no.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.200
Of course she did!

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.650
Ah, that's so good.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.360
Changing up one's situation 
can be pretty nice.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.500
I'm so sorry.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.870
Let's go home.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.250
Jeez...

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.960
Wait, so you like being in there?

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:07.400
Yeah. It's quite comfortable in here.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.100
You mean you took her away 
while she was sleeping?

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.320
That's terrifying.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.230
You're like a demon sometimes, Akari.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:20.030
The sea was almost the last sight I ever saw.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.400
I'm sorry.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.930
I just wanted to share my precious 
summer break with you.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.120
I appreciate that, but still...

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.420
Isn't there some kind of summer 
activity we could enjoy together?

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.040
The pool's no good.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.850
Rivers are no good.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.020
We can't go to any outdoor events.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.760
Hey, what if we do some dares?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.060
What does that mean?

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.890
It's a traditional summer pastime in Japan.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.560
You visit graves and stuff.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.700
Oh, that sounds like fun!

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.430
You go at night, so you both should be fine.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.130
No!

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.710
If there are ghosts, it'll be scary!

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.700
Yeah, I guess so...

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:13.290
<i>I thought I could spend all day with 
Sophie-chan once it was summer break.</i>

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.020
I'm glad you're at home all the time.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.040
<i>If I think about it, though, 
she's asleep during the day.</i>

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.550
<b>Quiet...</b>

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.400
I wish she'd wake up already.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.020
A storm?

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.450
I guess this <i>is</i> summer.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.700
Maybe I'll sleep a little more.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.290
Good morning, Sophie-chan!

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.510
Mornin—

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.320
You slept in late today.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:15.250
Yeah...

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:21.760
I was thinking I should adjust my sleep
 schedule to yours over summer break.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.740
I wouldn't do that.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.360
Humans have a rhythm that suits them best.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:37.170
Once, I tried waking up at 6 AM and 
going to bed at 10 PM for a while.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.810
What a refreshing morning.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.420
I'll do some cleaning while 
the sun is still out.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.630
Oh, Sophie-chan. Going out?

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:54.450
Just a short walk before dinner.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:59.670
Why? Why do I feel so alert 
and unable to sleep?

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.430
It's always bright outside.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.690
And thus, little by little,
 I started to get depressed.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.360
But that seems like such  
a healthy schedule.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:17.900
Ta-da!

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.870
I made you a summery shaved ice!

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.330
I brought the shaved ice machine we've been 
using since I was little from my house!

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.680
<b>Freeze</b>

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.670
So cold...

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.650
There's a lot more, so eat up!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.660
The shaved ice maker is terrifying!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.850
I guess it melted a bit...

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.120
It's hot even in the evening 
this time of year.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.900
Sophie-chan, aren't you hot
 in those long sleeves?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.520
Since vampires don't have a body 
temperature like humans do,

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.870
wearing clothes doesn't 
actually make us warmer.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.440
I see...

00:07:58.440 --> 00:07:59.320
Oh!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:07.510
So that means you're nice and cool, 
and doing this will feel good.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:09.630
You're smothering me. Stop it.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:11.720
That reminds me.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.840
The flowers I planted in the 
garden are blooming nicely.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.190
You should see them!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.670
S-Sure...

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.640
<b>Wilt...</b>

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.600
So this is "nicely"?

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:27.940
<b>* Morning glory</b>

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.070
Is this what you call "wabi-sabi"?

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.050
How deep.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.870
They looked so pretty this morning.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.900
I forgot they don't bloom at night.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.160
If you look at them in sunlight,
 they're really pretty.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:45.410
This time of year, sunflowers and 
hollyhock are really vibrant.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:49.940
It's too bright during the day, and I can't 
really make out the colors of the flowers.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.890
Then next time, I'll plant some 
in a pot and put them inside!

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.600
No, it's fine.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.590
Huh?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.310
I don't like flowers. They wilt so quickly.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.130
Sophie-chan?

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.220
Good evening.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.890
Welcome, Ellie-chan!

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.730
What are you two doing in the garden?

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:17.490
Ellie, you might have been invited in once,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.500
but can't you come in through the gate?

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.950
It just rained, and I didn't 
want to get my shoes wet.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.520
That's not a good reason.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.800
Can't we just go inside?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.640
Hey, wait!

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:35.890
Isn't there anything summery 
I can enjoy with Sophie-chan?

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:39.510
<i>Yuri-chan, hurry up! It's about to start!</i>

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:42.910
<i>Wait, Miki! I can't run in this outfit!</i>

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.000
You're watching those moving pictures again?

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:46.850
<i>Don't worry! You've got the 
track team's ace on your side!</i>

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.380
It's anime. I had a bunch recorded, 
so I thought I should watch it.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.380
<i>Uh, what does that have to do with it?</i>

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:51.110
<i>Miki-chan, over here!</i>

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:55.120
<i>Wow, it's so pretty!</i>

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>Wait... I'm not ready for that yet.</i>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.100
Kimono?

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.810
Is this a period drama?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.280
<i>You two are late.</i>

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.500
No, those are yukata.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.780
<i>I already ate all the cotton candy, 
yakisoba, takoyaki, and shaved ice.</i>

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.120
In Japan, they wear those to festivals.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:06.560
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.190
A fireworks show...

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.040
This is it!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.380
It's something you do at night, 
and it's a summer thing.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.290
It's perfect!

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.900
Now that that's decided, 
I need to get our yukata ready.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.460
I don't know what's going on,
 but it looks fun.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.690
Oh, it's cosplay!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:33.760
Good morning.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.270
Good morning, Sophie-chan!

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.330
A yukata!

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.740
The fireworks show is tonight!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.690
Right, that's today.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.370
Let's get you changed!

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.390
I'll help you dress.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:49.710
Okay, thanks.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.180
It's done!

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:53.540
How does it look?

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.850
It really suits you!

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.280
How do you like the yukata?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.350
Is something wrong with it?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:08.610
Well, it's just that vampires aren't 
alive, so I was wondering

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:11.190
if it's still okay to have the 
left side go over the right.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:14.220
That's such a small detail.
Don't worry about it.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.820
Besides, people will just think 
you put it on wrong.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.350
Hey, Sophie! The kimono looks great.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.320
I already told you, it's a yukata.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.400
Is mine done, too?

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.400
Of course!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.150
Then hand it over!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.350
Well? Do I look good?

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:35.810
Ellie-chan, you look lovely!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:36.740
Adorable!

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:38.370
You look just like a doll.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.700
This seems hard to walk in, though.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.080
That's improper.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.800
We don't do this every day, so why 
don't we make our feet cute, too?

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.990
There's still time until the show, 
so I'll give you a pedicure.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.480
Stop twitching. I can't paint them like that.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.590
I can't move?

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.390
<i>Must not move... Must not move...</i>

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:00.350
Sophie's feet are very ticklish.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.350
What?

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:06.390
<i>Discovering someone's weakness is... great.</i>

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.880
There it is again...

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.570
That demon I sometimes
 sense inside Akari.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.360
Heya!

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.540
Are you all read— Oh!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:15.700
Yeah!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.910
We're all ready to go.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.660
You're all in yukata!

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.270
I made them myself.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.650
They look good, huh?

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:23.790
They do!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.560
What's wrong, Hinata?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.840
Oh, nothing. Ready to go?

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.010
<i>I'm jealous that they all 
look so good in yukata.</i>

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.730
<i>I wish I was a bit more feminine...</i>

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:36.770
<i>Just kidding.</i>

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.780
Wait!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.320
Huh?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.640
You're not ready yet.

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:47.270
I made you a yukata, too!

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.040
No, I'm not...

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.030
You have no say in this.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:53.760
Wait!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:00.920
<b>Fireworks Festival</b>

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.750
Wow, it's really crowded!

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:09.180
This reminds me of Bastille Day.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.350
<b>Submit</b>

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:10.060
<b>A</b>

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:10.310
<b>At th</b>

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:10.640
<b>At the</b>

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:10.850
<b>At the fire</b>

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:11.310
<b>At the fireworks</b>

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:11.640
<b>At the fireworks sh</b>

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:11.770
<b>At the fireworks show</b>

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.100
<b>At the fireworks show!</b>

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:12.350
<b>At the fireworks show!!</b>

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.280
I feel like such a normie.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.660
Hinata-chan, hurry up!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.060
What's wrong?

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.560
Why are you fidgeting?

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:25.650
I-I haven't worn a yukata 
since I was a little kid.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.520
I feel so self-conscious.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.990
<i>But Akari made this just for me.</i>

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:34.870
<i>It fits perfectly.</i>

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:36.950
I think I'm happy.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.900
<i>You're happy that you're self-conscious?</i>

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.590
<i>That's weird.</i>

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.300
<i>So Hinata's into that sort of thing, huh?</i>

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:48.800
We all have different values, 
and that's a good thing.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.130
What are you talking about?

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.550
There are so many booths.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.000
There's all sorts of them!

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.600
I got some cotton candy and a candy apple.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.070
Both of those are candy.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.460
Says the person who got 
takoyaki and grilled squid.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.190
Festivals always have so much good food.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.440
Good food?

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.120
Like blood candy?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:19.460
<b>Chilled Blood</b>

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:19.460
<b>Delicious Blood</b>

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.750
Or chilled blood?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.460
I don't think they'll have anything like that.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.350
Sophie, look at the fishies swimming around!

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:25.840
These are goldfish. 
You scoop them out as a game.

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:30.190
So you're rescuing these 
fish from the stall's owner?

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.760
Here, on the house. Come play again!

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:33.170
I guess that's not <i>wrong</i>...

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.170
Wow, thanks!

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.650
Sophie-chan, that's amazing!

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.870
We're vampires, and it's night.

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:41.450
Catching fish like these is child's play.

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:43.580
You didn't catch any.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.210
You can have these, Akari.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.020
Oh, thank you!

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.990
But we don't have an aquarium.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.110
What should we do?

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:51.800
Aquarium?

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.960
I'll need a bunch of things 
if we're going to keep them.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:58.900
You mean you don't eat the goldfish with rice?

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:00.130
No, you don't!

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:08.580
Huh?

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:10.240
What's wrong, Yuu?

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.520
I could've sworn I just saw Sophie-san.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.750
Really? Sophie-chan?

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.280
She was wearing a yukata, 
though, so it probably wasn't her.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:21.410
Sis, I want some baby castella!

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:22.140
Okay.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:28.910
Wow!

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:29.670
That's amazing.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:30.750
It's so pretty!

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.460
Isn't it beautiful?

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:35.810
It is!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.270
It <i>is</i> beautiful,

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:43.000
but what's the point of spending 
all this energy and money

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.550
on flowers that disappear in an instant?

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:47.240
This cost-performance index is lousy.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.630
That's not true.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:49.630
Huh?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:55.310
They vanish in an instant, but they'll 
stay in our memories forever.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:57.020
It's not pointless.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.870
That's why I'm glad I got to 
see the fireworks with you.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.590
I see.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.380
Are you blushing?

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:19.870
<b>Lovey-dovey</b>

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.620
What about me?! What about <i>me</i>?!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.250
I'm glad I got to see it with you, too!

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.750
What's that?

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:27.990
Is someone flying?

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.460
Japan has such pretty fireworks, too!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.250
Stop flying!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:39.390
And up here, I'm so close to them!
They're so pretty!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.390
There are going to be more weird rumors!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:44.030
You think we really fooled them about Ellie?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:46.710
Vampires fly. It's what they <i>do</i>.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.050
Now, listen...

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:54.020
I hope we can see the fireworks together 
again next year, and every year after that.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:55.750
That would be nice.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:56.870
Right?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.240
It'd be great if we were always together.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:06.090
<i>Does this mean Akari will stay by my side
 forever, without ever getting a boyfriend?!</i>

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.560
What's wrong, Hinata-chan?

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.870
Nothing. Go on ahead without me.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.900
Look, Sophie-chan, this is for you.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:21.850
What is it?

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:25.310
I made a bookmark with 
a pressed morning glory.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:29.780
This one won't wilt or shrivel 
at night, and it's practical!

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:32.530
You're right. Thank you.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:37.840
<i>These days I wouldn't use this, since 
I almost exclusively read ebooks,</i>

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:39.400
<i>but I won't mention that.</i>

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:50.980
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:50.980
<b>The Last Day of Summer Break</b>

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.640
<i>I'm standing alone under this tree.</i>

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:23.090
<i>I don't have anything in particular with me.</i>

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:23.880
<i>Which means...</i>

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:32.330
<i>I can't take even a single step.</i>

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.550
<i>This all started that time I went on a walk.</i>

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.390
I'll just rest a bit here.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.320
<i>A sunflower?</i>

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.110
<i>Maybe some kids were playing with it.</i>

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:58.540
<i>I wonder how many seeds it has.</i>

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.580
<i>Seeing something like this really 
makes me want to start counting.</i>

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:05.730
One...

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:12.560
<b>A peculiar trait of vampires</b>

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:07.960
Two...

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:09.360
Three...

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:10.990
Four...

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.560
Five...

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.810
One hundred and ninety-seven...

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.410
One hundred and ninety-eight...

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:17.810
One hundred and ninety-nine...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:18.870
Two hundred...

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.830
Five hundred and twelve...

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.410
Five hundred and thirteen...

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.110
Five hundred and fourteen...

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.320
Eight hundred and eighty-eight...

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.120
Eight hundred and eighty-nine...

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.460
Eight hundred and ninety...

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.810
One thousand, two hundred and twenty-nine...

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.530
One thousand, two hundred and thirty...

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:35.650
One thousand, two hundred and thirty-one.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.520
I finally counted them all.

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.590
It's totally morning!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.820
I didn't even notice.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.040
<i>Obviously, I have neither 
my cloak nor my parasol.</i>

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:49.920
<i>I didn't bring my phone, either.</i>

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:53.550
<i>Isn't there any way for me to leave?</i>

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.770
<i>I have a single 500 yen coin with me.</i>

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.620
<i>Could I buy an umbrella with this?</i>

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.090
<i>Probably not.</i>

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:05.320
<i>Ones that aren't transparent
 plastic are more expensive.</i>

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.000
<i>I could call Akari on a pay phone 
and ask her to bring me a parasol.</i>

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.800
<i>Wait, do they still have pay phones?</i>

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:19.430
<i>As long as I'm stuck under this tree,</i>

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:22.340
<i>having some change won't 
do me any good anyway.</i>

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>I guess I've got no choice but to 
wait here until the sun goes down.</i>

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.360
<i>I'm getting sleepy...</i>

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:37.600
<i>I don't have anything to do,
so I guess I'll take a little nap.</i>

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:46.650
Giraffe blood is just as sweet as I imagined.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:49.900
Yup, capybara blood is gross...

00:21:54.820 --> 00:21:56.630
<i>If I fall asleep, I'll die!</i>

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.570
<i>The sun is getting stronger.</i>

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:08.310
<i>How many more hours am I going to 
have to stay out here by myself?</i>

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:12.840
This is harder than I thought.

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:22.430
Sophie-chan, there you are!

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:27.100
I came to collect you.

00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:29.830
Collect me?

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:31.180
Are you the grim reaper?

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:33.320
No! It's me!

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:38.530
I'm so glad I found you!

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:39.970
Akari, is that you?

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:42.430
It was so bright, I couldn't really see you.

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:46.060
You weren't home in the morning, 
and I started to worry

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:49.850
that maybe something happened to you 
while you were out on your walk!

00:22:49.850 --> 00:22:52.170
Oh. I'm really sorry.

00:22:55.130 --> 00:22:57.580
Shall we go home, then?

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:03.570
Yeah, let's go.

00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:06.410
Oh! I'm so sorry!

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:10.420
I was in such a rush, I didn't 
bring your parasol or anything.

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:13.180
I'll go get it.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:17.280
It's fine.

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:20.700
Please just stay here.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:30.040
The shade feels so nice, 
and this juice is so cold!

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.360
Good thing I had that change.

00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:38.350
<i>We ended up staying until the sun went down,
 and then walked home together.</i>
